<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?latexml class="article"?>
<?latexml RelaxNGSchema="LaTeXML"?>
<document xmlns="http://dlmf.nist.gov/LaTeXML" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <resource src="LaTeXML.css" type="text/css"/>
  <para xml:id="p1">
    <p>The RDFa set, plus an image fallback, on a display formula:
      <Math mode="display" class="ltx_my_math" tex="x+y" text="x + y" about="#thm1" resource="#eq1" property="ex:formula" rel="ex:partOf" rev="ex:hasPart" typeof="ex:Equation" datatype="xsd:string" content="x plus y" imagesrc="eq1.png" imagewidth="42" imageheight="17" imagedepth="5" xml:id="p1.m1"><XMath>
          <XMApp>
            <XMTok meaning="plus" role="ADDOP">+</XMTok>
            <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">x</XMTok>
            <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">y</XMTok>
          </XMApp>
        </XMath><m:math about="#thm1" altimg="eq1.png" altimg-height="17px" altimg-valign="-5px" altimg-width="42px" alttext="x+y" class="ltx_my_math" content="x plus y" datatype="xsd:string" display="block" property="ex:formula" rel="ex:partOf" resource="#eq1" rev="ex:hasPart" typeof="ex:Equation"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></Math>
    </p>
    <p>An inline formula with NO image and NO RDFa, so neither attribute family
      may be invented:
      <Math mode="inline" tex="z" text="z" xml:id="p1.m2"><XMath>
          <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">z</XMTok>
        </XMath><m:math alttext="z" display="inline"><m:mi>z</m:mi></m:math></Math>
    </p>
    <p>An image with NO depth, so altimg-valign must be omitted rather than
      emitted as a bare minus sign:
      <Math mode="inline" tex="w" text="w" imagesrc="eq2.png" imagewidth="9" imageheight="8" xml:id="p1.m3"><XMath>
          <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">w</XMTok>
        </XMath><m:math altimg="eq2.png" altimg-height="8px" altimg-width="9px" alttext="w" display="inline"><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:math></Math>
    </p>
  </para>
</document>
